    /// THE UNCAGED ROLES ARE UNCAGED TOGETHER — the five studios, and `director`.
    ///
    /// It used to be the exception, and that was never a decision: `designer` was already a session
    /// role when roles were mapped onto namespaces, while `architect`, `librarian`, `sound-designer`
    /// and `integrator` were not — so the designer became the only caged studio by name collision.
    /// In that cage every session died on its first instructed command (`bsc: command not found`),
    /// because its whole documented surface is `bsc ui` and this module refuses to bind `bsc`.
    ///
    /// This pins them together so none can quietly rejoin the set. `director` is the newest member
    /// and arrived by the same route: caged, it died `exit=1` on `bsc: command not found`. Re-adding it is a
    /// real decision with a precondition — the caged surface has to be able to do the job first
    /// (`complete-the-caged-designer-surface`) — and that decision should break this test and be
    /// made here, not slip in as a one-line parser entry.
    #[test]
    fn the_uncaged_roles_are_uncaged_together() {
        // Driven from the CONSTANT rather than a list repeated here: the constant is where the
        // decision and its per-role reason live, so a role removed from it to be caged breaks this
        // test at the same moment, instead of leaving a stale duplicate that still passes.
        assert!(!UNCAGED_ROLES.is_empty(), "the set must not silently empty out");
        for (name, store, blocker) in UNCAGED_ROLES {
            assert!(
                Role::parse(name).is_none(),
                "{name} must NOT resolve to a namespace profile — these run uncaged until the caged \
                 surface can do their job. Re-adding one is a decision; make it here.",
            );
            // The reason has to be a REASON. "Leave it uncaged" is a legitimate answer only while it
            // is written down, and an entry with an empty store or an empty blocker is a TODO
            // wearing the shape of a decision.
            assert!(!store.trim().is_empty(), "{name} must name the store its surface writes");
            assert!(!blocker.trim().is_empty(), "{name} must name what the cage still lacks");
        }
        // ...and the profile it would use is still MODELLED, so completing the cage means filling in
        // a surface rather than re-deriving what a designer may touch.
        assert!(ALL_ROLES.contains(&Role::Designer));
        assert!(!Role::Designer.work_reaches_a_remote(), "still the one role that needs no remote");
    }

